# React architecture

## Layers (existing repo paths)

```text
src/components/ui/       design-system primitives (no business data)
src/components/shared/   cross-domain compositions + empty/loading/error
src/components/layout/   shell, nav, page chrome
src/features/            page compositions (home, experiences, booking, map, admin)
src/server/repositories/ Supabase access + Zod + view-model mapping
src/lib/view-models/     pure DB/RPC → UI mappers
```

Adapt to these folders; do not invent parallel conventions.

## Rules

- Server Components by default; `use client` only at the smallest interactive boundary.
- Presentational components: typed props / view models only — no Supabase, no privileged clients, no embedded experience/pricing records.
- Fetch in server components, route handlers, server actions, or repositories; map at the backend boundary.
- Lists: stable database IDs as keys (never indexes when an ID exists).
- Correct for zero, one, many records and missing optional media.
- Reuse shared states (price, duration, empty, loading, error) instead of copying page-specific UI.
- Design system only: CostaPulse tokens in `src/app/globals.css`; no arbitrary one-off styling when a token/primitive exists.
- New UI patterns need ≥2 real use cases (or are foundational primitives) before abstracting.
- Map/calendar must use `get_experience_map` / `get_experience_calendar` contracts; media via shared media utilities.
